# MiniDev UI rules

Start with `docs/VISION.md`. Our edge is Light and Material (one cursor light, four materials: hairline, glass, metal, paper), Blueprint (the spec ships with the component), Physics (things that move have mass) and Composition (always shown inside Lumen). Every component needs one named signature detail, springs from the preset table, even numbers only, and a Lumen demo.

You are building MiniDev UI: free, MIT, React 19 + Tailwind v4 + Base UI components, shadcn-compatible.
The bar is "a senior product designer screenshots it". Linear, Vercel, Stripe, Raycast quality.
The style is called Hairline: quiet surfaces, 1px lines, a top highlight, one violet accent used sparingly.

## Read before writing any component

1. `DESIGN.md` (the rules) and `src/styles/minidev.css` (every token that exists).
2. The gold-standard components. Copy their patterns, not just their colours:
   - `src/registry/ui/segmented-control.tsx`: motion indicator (layoutId), roving keyboard, sizes lookup, controlled + uncontrolled.
   - `src/registry/ui/otp-input.tsx`: one real input under painted slots, caret, glyph-in, shake on error.
   - `src/registry/ui/file-dropzone.tsx`: four drag states, SVG hairline border, async list with progress, error, retry, aria-live.
   - `src/registry/ui/data-table.tsx`: sort with aria-sort, selection with indeterminate, accent rail, hover actions, sticky header shadow, skeleton, floating bulk bar.
   - `src/registry/ui/toast.tsx`: imperative API plus a stacked, hover-to-expand system.
   - `src/registry/ui/number-roll.tsx`: identity-keyed digits on the roll spring.
   - `src/registry/ui/morph-panel.tsx`: a trigger that morphs into its panel.
   - Primitives: `button.tsx`, `input.tsx`, `checkbox.tsx`, `switch.tsx`, `tabs.tsx`.
3. `src/components/reference/demos.tsx`: how a demo looks (realistic data, a scenario, then states).

## Tokens (the only colours you may use)

Surfaces: `bg-bg` (page), `bg-surface` (cards, fields), `bg-raised` (menus, thumbs, popovers), `bg-sunken` (tracks, wells, hover fills).
Lines: `border-border` (default), `border-border-strong` (hover, filled), `bg-border` for 1px dividers.
Text: `text-fg`, `text-fg-muted` (secondary), `text-fg-subtle` (placeholder, meta).
Ink (primary action): `bg-ink text-on-ink shadow-ink hover:bg-ink-hover`.
Accent (violet, punctuation only): `bg-accent text-on-accent`, `text-accent-fg`, `bg-accent-soft`, `border-accent-line`, `ring-accent`.
Status: `success`, `warning`, `danger`, `info` (text-*, bg-*, border-*). For tints: `bg-[color-mix(in_oklch,var(--danger)_6%,var(--surface))]`.
Depth: `shadow-xs` (fields), `shadow-raised` (cards), `shadow-key` (outline buttons, keycaps, small tiles), `shadow-ink` (solid buttons), `shadow-overlay` (menus, popovers, dialogs, toasts). Nothing else.
Opacity tints of fg for hover fills: `hover:bg-fg/5`, pressed `bg-fg/[0.06]`.

Materials reach components only through these exact token classes. `bg-white`, `bg-surface/80` on cards, hand-written shadows and `backdrop-blur` on surfaces all break glass, metal and paper. Test with `?material=glass|metal|paper` in the URL.

Forbidden: hex, `bg-blue-500` style palette steps, `bg-muted`/`text-muted-foreground`/`bg-primary` (old shadcn names), gradients on UI surfaces, glassmorphism, blur shadows on cards, `transition-all`, `hover:scale-*`, `active:scale-*`, 2px borders, emoji in UI, new CSS variables, new npm packages.

## Recipes (paste these, do not improvise)

Field (input, select trigger, combobox, textarea):
`h-9 rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface px-3 text-sm text-fg shadow-xs outline-none placeholder:text-fg-subtle transition-[border-color,box-shadow,background-color] duration-[140ms] ease-hairline hover:border-border-strong focus-visible:border-accent focus-visible:shadow-[0_0_0_3px_var(--accent-soft)] aria-invalid:border-danger disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:bg-sunken disabled:text-fg-muted`

Focus ring for buttons and clickable things:
`outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-bg`
(inside a sunken track use `ring-offset-1 ring-offset-sunken`)

Ghost icon button: `grid size-7 place-items-center rounded-md text-fg-subtle outline-none hover:bg-sunken hover:text-fg focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent`

Track (segmented, tabs, slider rail): `bg-sunken shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--border)]`
Thumb / selected segment: `bg-raised shadow-[0_1px_2px_0_oklch(0_0_0/0.08),0_0_0_1px_var(--border),inset_0_1px_0_0_var(--highlight)]`

Card: `rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface shadow-raised`
Overlay (menu, popover): `rounded-xl border border-border bg-raised p-1 shadow-overlay`
Menu item: `flex h-8 items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 text-[0.8125rem] text-fg outline-none data-[highlighted]:bg-sunken`
Kbd hint: use `<Kbd>` from `@/registry/ui/kbd`.
Selected row / item rail: `bg-accent-soft shadow-[inset_2px_0_0_var(--accent)]`
Hit area on small controls: `relative after:absolute after:-inset-2` (min 44px touch target).

## Geometry and type

Heights: 28 (xs), 32 (sm), 36 (default), 44 (lg), 48 (xl). Radius: controls `rounded-lg`, cards `rounded-xl`, overlays `rounded-xl`/`rounded-2xl`, inner items `rounded-md`. Nested radius = outer minus padding.
Spacing on a 4px grid. Dense UI text is `text-[0.8125rem]` (13px), meta `text-xs`, labels `font-medium`.
Numbers: `tabular-nums`. IDs, keys, code, file extensions: `font-mono`.
Never centre long text. Headings `text-balance`.

## Motion

Colour changes `duration-[70ms]`. Transform and shadow `duration-[140ms]`. Enter `duration-200`. Exit 160ms. Easing `ease-hairline`.
Anything that moves position, size or shape uses a spring preset from `docs/VISION.md` (snappy, morph, roll, release, data). Never invent new timings.
Always `const reduce = useReducedMotion()` and pass `{ duration: 0 }` when true.
Available keyframes: `rise-in`, `glyph-in`, `pop-in`, `shake-x`, `dash-march`, `caret-blink`, `shimmer-x`, `shimmer-text`, `pulse-ring`, `marquee`. Use as `animate-[pop-in_280ms_var(--ease-hairline)_both]`.
Press feedback: `active:translate-y-px` or a darker fill. Never scale.

## Component contract (every file in src/registry)

- `"use client"` at the top when it has state or handlers.
- Root element has `data-slot="<name>"` and accepts `className` (merged with `cn`).
- Controlled and uncontrolled: `value` + `defaultValue` + `onChange` (or `checked`/`open` equivalents).
- Renders something good with ZERO props. The docs page renders every component with no props. Use realistic defaults.
- Every state is designed, in light and dark: rest, hover, pressed, focus-visible, disabled, loading, empty, error/invalid, selected, read-only where it applies.
- Keyboard follows the WAI-ARIA APG pattern for its role. Base UI primitives already do this; use them (`@base-ui/react/*`) instead of hand-rolling menus, popovers, dialogs, selects, sliders.
- Async changes announced with an `aria-live="polite"` sr-only span.
- Export the component and its props type: `export { Thing }; export type { ThingProps }`.
- Never break an existing export or prop. Before changing a signature, search for usages (`rg "<Thing"`) and keep old props working.
- Sample copy is for a fictional SaaS called Lumen (invoices, customers, deploys, workspaces). No lorem ipsum, no "Premium", no MiniDev marketing copy inside components, no em dashes.

## Checks (run after every component)

```
npm run registry
npx tsc --noEmit
npm run craft -- <file-name>
```
`npm run craft` must show 0 errors for your files. Fix warnings in files you touched.
Then look at it: `npm run dev`, open `/gallery/<slug>` and `/docs/<name>`, both themes (header toggle), and at 390px wide. No horizontal scroll.
